From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:17:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq25890: keep the charging guard's
 limits across a suspend

The guard holds charging off, or the OTG boost on, by kicking the
chip's 40 s watchdog every 10 s. Asleep it cannot, and when the
watchdog expires the chip restores its defaults: charging on, boost
off. A suspend with a charger attached would then charge past the
owner's limit, and one with the boost on would cut a USB device's
power.

With a charger attached the system runs from it and a suspend saves
nothing, so refuse to suspend then, and while the boost is on. On the
battery, stop the guard's work for the suspend, since its I2C bus is
going down, and run a pass at resume, which also notices a charger
attached in the meantime.

A charger attached while suspended still charges unguarded until the
next resume. Closing that needs either a wakeup on attach or the chip's
watchdog off for the suspend, a write the guard does not make today.
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c
index d179b38ff..a1cb5475e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq25890_charger.c
@@ -1876,6 +1876,29 @@ static int bq25890_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct bq25890_device *bq = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
+	if (bq->guard_battery) {
+		int otg = bq25890_field_read(bq, F_OTG_CFG);
+
+		mutex_lock(&bq->lock);
+		__bq25890_handle_irq(bq);
+		mutex_unlock(&bq->lock);
+
+		/*
+		 * The guard holds its limits by feeding the chip's 40 s
+		 * watchdog; asleep it cannot, and the expiry restores the
+		 * defaults: charging on, boost off. With a charger attached
+		 * the system runs from it and has nothing to save, so stay
+		 * awake while one is, or while the boost powers a device.
+		 */
+		if (bq->state.online || otg) {
+			dev_info(bq->dev, "guard: %s, refusing to suspend\n",
+				 otg ? "OTG boost on" : "charger attached");
+			return -EBUSY;
+		}
+
+		disable_delayed_work_sync(&bq->guard_work);
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * If charger is removed, while in suspend, make sure ADC is diabled
 	 * since it consumes slightly more power.
@@ -1907,6 +1930,12 @@ static int bq25890_resume(struct device *dev)
 unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&bq->lock);
 
+	/* A pass now: a charger may have been attached while asleep. */
+	if (bq->guard_battery) {
+		enable_delayed_work(&bq->guard_work);
+		mod_delayed_work(system_power_efficient_wq, &bq->guard_work, 0);
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 #endif
-- 
